course: dictionary
lesson: 2400
title: Curve: a line that bends
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A curve is a line that bends smoothly, with no sharp corners, like part of a circle. The word can be a noun (a curve) or a verb (to curve). Context clues help you see which one it is.
explain: «Let go of a ball swung on a string and it flies off in a straight line, not in a curve.» The sentence tells you what a curve is not: a straight line. When the ball is let go, it flies straight, so the curve was the bendy path the ball made while it was swung round.
explain: In maths, a graph line can curve, and in safety lessons a curve in the road is a clue to be careful. «You cross roads away from curves, because drivers cannot see you.» A bend hides you from drivers, so you need to take care there.
fact: A curve is a line that bends smoothly, without sharp corners.
fact: Circles and ovals are made of curves.
fact: A bend in a road, river or path can also be called a curve.
fact: «Curve» can be a noun (a curve, curves) or a verb (curve, curved, curving).
fact: Useful phrases: «a curved line», «a sharp curve», «curve around», «around the curve».
exercise: «Let go of a ball swung on a string and it flies off in a straight line, not in a curve.» What is a curve? | A flat, square shape | A dot on a page | A straight line from one end to the other | *A line that bends smoothly without sharp corners
exercise: Why do we cross roads away from a curve? | Curves are the fastest part of the road | Curves are always wet and slippery | Cars never go round curves | *Drivers cannot see you round the bend
exercise: Find and copy the word that means a bend in the sentence: «The river takes a sudden curve past the old mill.» | takes | mill | river | *curve
test: «Mia drew a curved line, like half of a circle.» What does curved mean here? | Broken into pieces | *Bent smoothly, with no sharp corners | Straight and flat | Coloured in with paint
test: «The path curves to the left after the bridge.» What does curves mean here? | Shines brightly in the sun | *Bends in a smooth line | Falls off the edge | Stops suddenly
exam: Which shape is made of curves, not straight lines? | *A circle | A square | A triangle | A rectangle
